commit 81c250d70664a896b0595ac810758c15b81087a3
Author: Francis Townsend-Merino <townsendmerino@gmail.com>
Date:   Mon Sep 28 14:08:39 2026 -0700

    deps: aikit v1.50.2 (amd64 AVX2 activation quantizer) in every module
    
    v1.50.2 vectorizes quantizeRowInt8Core's two scalar passes on amd64 (S-03's arm64/NEON half
    shipped 2026-09-03; amd64 was left open) -- the amd64 half of the goinfer investigation into why
    CPU decode's `down` matmul streams slower per byte than `gate+up`
    (docs/measurements/cpu-down-vs-gateup-bandwidth-2026-09-28.md). Bit-identical, mutation-checked on
    the aikit side; perfgate PASS vs v1.50.1, BenchmarkQuantizeRowInt8 independently re-measured
    10.9x/21.2x faster at K=1536/K=8960. Two x86 ISA differences from ARM64 found and fixed along the
    way (VMAXPS's asymmetric NaN rule, VCVTTPS2DQ's fixed indefinite-value overflow behaviour) -- see
    the aikit v1.50.2 CHANGELOG for both.
    
    Verified against the REAL published module (GOWORK=off, no local override): a 1.5B CPU greedy
    generation (80 tokens, temp=0) is text-identical to the pre-bump build; the down/gate+up
    decode-time split reads 2.98/6.02, 8.91/18.13, 40.84/82.62 ms/token (0.5B/1.5B/7B) -- the same
    ballpark as the exploratory go.work numbers in the measurement doc.
    
    gofmt, go vet (root, realckpt, cuda goinfer_testhooks, gpu goinfer_testhooks): clean.
    
    non-numeric core refresh; validated_at preserved.
    forward goldens green at 2c8ce082 on arch=amd64: 62 passed / 0 skipped / 0 failed.
    
    Deps-Hash-Refresh: 2c8ce082 goldens=62 arch=amd64
    
    The paired bench_peer speed gate (the real ship/park bar for a speed claim) is still queued for
    tonight (avx2quant-cpu-speed); this bump does not wait on it -- owner: "do the aikit pr and
    release now, i don't want to wait". Every gate that CAN run today (aikit's full CI matrix, both
    release-gate and consumer-resolution on the tag, this repo's own parity goldens) is green.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

